==================================================================
DAY 24 - PART A: THEORY
Volumes: emptyDir, hostPath, and Why Pod Storage Is Ephemeral
Time: 30-40 minutes
==================================================================

1. THE PROBLEM (AGAIN)
----------------------
Day 2: a container's writable layer disappears with the container.
In Kubernetes it's worse: containers restart, pods get rescheduled to
other nodes, Deployments replace pods all the time.

A VOLUME is a directory mounted into a pod's containers whose lifetime
is NOT tied to a single container.


2. HOW VOLUMES ARE DECLARED
---------------------------
Two parts:
  spec.volumes                         (pod level: what it is)
  spec.containers[].volumeMounts       (container: where to mount)

  spec:
    volumes:
    - name: scratch
      emptyDir: {}
    containers:
    - name: app
      volumeMounts:
      - name: scratch
        mountPath: /tmp/work
        readOnly: false


3. VOLUME TYPES BY LIFETIME
---------------------------
Lives as long as the POD:
  emptyDir      empty directory created when the pod starts on a node;
                shared by all containers in the pod; survives container
                restarts; DELETED when the pod is removed.
                emptyDir.medium: Memory -> tmpfs (RAM, counts against
                memory limit). sizeLimit to cap usage.
  configMap / secret / downwardAPI / projected   (Days 22-23)

Lives as long as the NODE:
  hostPath      a path on the node's filesystem. Data stays on that
                node only. If the pod moves to another node, it sees
                different (or no) data. Security risk: can expose the
                node (/, /var/run/docker.sock). Used by system
                DaemonSets (log collectors, CNI), avoid for apps.

Lives independently (survives pods AND nodes):
  persistentVolumeClaim   -> PV backed by network/cloud storage (Day 25)


4. emptyDir USE CASES
---------------------
  - share files between containers in a pod (sidecar, Day 9)
  - scratch space / cache
  - checkpoint data that may survive a container crash (not pod loss)


5. hostPath TYPES
-----------------
  type: Directory          must already exist
  type: DirectoryOrCreate  create if missing
  type: File / FileOrCreate / Socket ...


6. EPHEMERAL STORAGE LIMITS
---------------------------
Container logs, writable layer and emptyDir use the node's disk
("ephemeral storage"). You can request and limit it:
  resources:
    requests:
      ephemeral-storage: 1Gi
    limits:
      ephemeral-storage: 2Gi
Exceeding the limit = pod evicted.


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- volumes (pod) + volumeMounts (container).
- emptyDir dies with the pod; hostPath stays on one node.
- Real persistence needs PersistentVolumes (tomorrow).
